{#- VESTA message layout — the VESTA Agent's one layout (vesta_shared/message_format.py), for the alerts Home Assistant
    sends itself, with telegram_bot.send_message parse_mode: html. Copy to /config/custom_templates/, then call the
    action homeassistant.reload_custom_templates.

    Used by INCLUDE, never import, and always "ignore missing": a missing file renders nothing and the blueprint sends
    its plain text instead — an alert never depends on this file.
        {%- set vm_title, vm_to, vm_text, vm_status = '🔥 Mains phase overload', 'Owner', 'Phase C 4450 W', '⚠️ New alert' -%}
        {% include 'vesta_message.jinja' ignore missing %}
    gives:
        <b>🔥 Mains phase overload</b>
        To: Owner
        <blockquote>Phase C 4450 W</blockquote>

        Status:
        <blockquote><i>⚠️ New alert</i></blockquote>

    "To:" is vm_to when a rule names who it is for; empty, it is the villa-wide input_text.vesta_alert_audience (one
    place for every alert, owner 2026-10-12). It is a ROLE, as the agent writes it (message_format.audience; owner,
    2026-10-13: "To: Owner", "To: Facility Manager" or "To: Owner & Facility Manager", never a name): any other value —
    a name, the helper missing — is "Owner & Facility Manager".

    The bottom line is said by its STAGE, in the agent's own words (architecture review, 2026-10-13: a job's Done read
    "✅ Done - JM" here and "✅ Done pressed by JM on 12/10/2026 17:13." under the agent's alerts). A rule sets
    vm_stage — 'new', 'existing', 'closed' or 'help' — and this file writes its icon (message_format.STAGE_ICONS,
    MARK_ICONS) before vm_status, or the stage's own words when there is no status (STAGE_WORDS). With vm_who (who
    pressed Done or Need help), the line says it as the agent does (PRESSED), then vm_status:
        {%- set vm_stage, vm_who, vm_status = 'help', 'JM', 'Tick it on the Jobs tab.' -%}
        →  🆘 Need help pressed by JM on 13/10/2026 09:02. Tick it on the Jobs tab.
    Without vm_stage, vm_status is written as it is (a rule saved before 2026-10-13).

    The tags are the agent's style table (message_format.TELEGRAM: title bold, item blockquote, note blockquote +
    italic); its test (tests/test_ha_message_layout.py) fails when this file and the agent's layout or words differ.
    Text is escaped here, once: Telegram's HTML refuses a bare "<", ">" or "&". -#}
{%- macro vm_escape(s) -%}{{ (s | default('', true) | string | trim) | replace('&', '&amp;') | replace('<', '&lt;') | replace('>', '&gt;') }}{%- endmacro -%}
{%- set vm_r = vm_to | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- if not vm_r and states is defined -%}{%- set vm_r = states('input_text.vesta_alert_audience') | trim -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set vm_roles = ['Owner', 'Facility Manager', 'Owner & Facility Manager'] -%}
{%- if vm_r not in vm_roles -%}{%- set vm_r = vm_roles[-1] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set vm_t = vm_text | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- set vm_s = vm_status | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- set vm_icons = {'new': '⚠️', 'existing': '⚠️ ⚙️', 'closed': '✅', 'help': '🆘'} -%}
{%- set vm_words = {'new': 'New alert', 'existing': 'Still open', 'closed': 'Closed: nothing more to do'} -%}
{%- set vm_g = vm_stage | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- if vm_g in vm_icons -%}
{%- set vm_p = vm_who | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- if vm_p -%}
{%- set vm_at = now().strftime('%d/%m/%Y %H:%M') if now is defined else '' -%}
{%- set vm_said = '{label} pressed by {name} on {time}.' | replace('{label}', 'Need help' if vm_g == 'help' else 'Done') | replace('{name}', vm_p) | replace('{time}', vm_at) -%}
{%- set vm_s = (vm_said ~ ' ' ~ vm_s) | trim -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set vm_s = vm_icons[vm_g] ~ ' ' ~ (vm_s or vm_words.get(vm_g, '')) -%}
{%- endif -%}
<b>{{ vm_escape(vm_title) }}</b>
To: {{ vm_escape(vm_r) }}
{%- if vm_t %}
<blockquote>{{ vm_escape(vm_t) }}</blockquote>
{%- endif %}
{%- if vm_s %}

Status:
<blockquote><i>{{ vm_escape(vm_s) }}</i></blockquote>
{%- endif %}
